      "text": "In Toronto, Canada, advance voting for the 2026 municipal election concluded on October 11, 2026, at 7 p.m. According to the City of Toronto, 222,550 eligible voters participated during the six days of advance voting. CBC Toronto reports this represents the largest turnout in over a decade and a nearly 72 per cent increase compared to the 129,000 early votes recorded during the 2023 mayoral byelection. Election day is scheduled for October 26, 2026. On that day, eligible voters must cast ballots at their assigned voting locations as indicated on their Voter Information Card or the Toronto Elections webpage. Voters who requested to vote by mail were required to return completed packages to Toronto Elections by October 7, 2026. To meet this deadline, the city advised using one of 25 secure, indoor yellow drop boxes located in each ward, which are monitored by CCTV and emptied daily by staff. Additionally, registration for third party advertisers, including any person, corporation, or trade union intending to spend money to promote or oppose a candidate, closed at 4:30 p.m. on October 9, 2026. Registrations were to be filed in person at the Toronto Elections City Hall office."
